69860.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F$ shown above, and let $C$ be the path where the curve is traversed from $A$ to $B.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$\n- ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ gives the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along $C:$\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true, while statement II is false. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ assists the motion of the particle as it moves from $A$ to $B.$\n\n![](images/c0/c075bf6fa60af07e70569395b257d25bb53f5edab8ff14f4a772271c9df7e153.png)\n\n \nSo, ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- Statement III is false. It's clear from the picture below that if we reverse the orientation of $C,$ then $F$ works against the motion of the particle as it moves from $B$ to $A.$\n\n![](images/41/41528079b285fb3ba20fcac0bd28f42ed7981a775938286654cf7319c1e8a6c6.png)\n\n \nSo, ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259845 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "77d82670-955d-5fbd-bc9e-ff9b5595ca19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463536} {:answer/id #uuid "70953006-86df-56ba-885e-a59756ac68a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463537}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "77d82670-955d-5fbd-bc9e-ff9b5595ca19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463536} :answer-field/id #uuid "4bbc6ae6-a433-51b7-9bcc-4234a55196ba" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464702} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e3413fb0-066c-5f24-a376-7d72fef132fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463538} {:answer/id #uuid "090b215e-b754-554a-8109-db90d4abfb27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463539}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "090b215e-b754-554a-8109-db90d4abfb27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463539} :answer-field/id #uuid "79b6f686-1017-5c39-b085-1d1f73f3ac2e" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464703} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f3c62597-d021-5cbd-8c81-864877afd3e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463540} {:answer/id #uuid "9d291d8d-f31c-5932-8efc-6cd6f690f503" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463541}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f3c62597-d021-5cbd-8c81-864877afd3e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463540} :answer-field/id #uuid "162bbeb9-8561-5809-b4fd-17fcbbfe7d72" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464704}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "e9d575c8-adec-5386-bb2f-10bc638decac" :question/math-academy-id "q-125706" :question/problem "![](images/a4/a423ab56220e438fb849d2025ab53b99bb74ef598e16110c911d691680130527.png)\n\nConsider the semicircle and constant vector field $F$ shown above. Let $C$ be the path where the semicircle is traversed from $A$ to $B.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$\n- ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ gives the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along $C:$\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statements I is false, while statement II is true. As the particle moves from $A$ to $B,$ the force $F$ works  against the particle for $x<0,$ while $F$  works with the particle for $x>0.$ \n\n![](images/cd/cd52e91c72d481980c9a48575da7ca3eaebd2ed27f96b1054cf5c1c5da1aa3d9.png)\n\n \nBy symmetry, the contribution to ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ for $x<0$ is canceled out by the contribution for $x>0.$ So, \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. If we reverse the orientation of $C,$ then the situation with regards to the work done by $F$ is similar to the previous case.\n\n![](images/a1/a1e8fa5262fc787b691b3753fc57ab39aceee7c57dbbe166c6da6f6effaf42dc.png)\n\n \nSo, ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275256 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32d3c794-0fd5-59cf-aa3b-e2dc7aaf04de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464402} {:answer/id #uuid "13f3080f-2a2e-5f68-ad93-0dc5cf51e7c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464403}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "32d3c794-0fd5-59cf-aa3b-e2dc7aaf04de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464402} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd59685b-e36e-57fc-b0de-87a808e2950e" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465135} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d3a5d282-29ec-5062-816b-49f4eab07dc0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464404} {:answer/id #uuid "058f6b84-807f-5c96-abd5-f5b7e248e1d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464405}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "058f6b84-807f-5c96-abd5-f5b7e248e1d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464405} :answer-field/id #uuid "2f03e31d-0bb7-55ed-a6f4-3f59148d1089" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465136} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ba0d7311-7b93-5e4b-a814-aa12d234796a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464406} {:answer/id #uuid "45d3662e-9e38-5c21-9f50-1fdddab0e3a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464407}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "45d3662e-9e38-5c21-9f50-1fdddab0e3a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464407} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a145f94-84f0-55f4-9b95-b1c537573877" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465137}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "08ceb92c-03d7-50b0-a12d-3ba81bdd7b99" :question/math-academy-id "q-150011" :question/problem "![](images/0d/0d2aa60719643235f5ae684d59607199731626e15bac40fd6b14d071c099ab4a.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F$ shown above, and let $C$ be the path along the segment $\\overset{―}{AB}$ traversed from $A$ to $B.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$\n- ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ gives the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along $C:$\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false, while statement II is true. It's clear from the picture below that $F$  works against the motion of the particle as it moves from $A$ to $B.$\n\n![](images/2b/2b8ef08638551571caa43150080a8550a0b61ed24eaa7c6da73fe66edd161e8e.png)\n\n \nSo, ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. It's clear from the picture below that if we reverse the orientation of $C,$ then $F$ assists the motion of the particle as it moves from $B$ to $A.$\n\n![](images/28/28db5c349d3455c58f81da7c181586ba4e0ad5662f35faa2575d6622b3713988.png)\n\n \nSo, ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414783 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "740bd403-f1e6-5a92-a2b9-efa1ee0f552f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472742} {:answer/id #uuid "5170cfef-7833-5d81-bf15-5bd1c2583c78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472743}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "740bd403-f1e6-5a92-a2b9-efa1ee0f552f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472742} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ab5fa05-0008-5864-bfbd-37a853fa3a21" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473766} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13931620-6744-5279-819c-a867d3d2f624" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472744} {:answer/id #uuid "89f7ef7d-3d29-5bcd-86e4-6ccb6a042395" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472745}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "89f7ef7d-3d29-5bcd-86e4-6ccb6a042395" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472745} :answer-field/id #uuid "0562aeab-6992-5c67-82d7-eee722fd8045" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473767} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "194dcf31-6ded-5f7d-8ad4-8503fc14610b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472746} {:answer/id #uuid "cff66d04-5359-528e-90cc-f15b10b85371" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472747}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "194dcf31-6ded-5f7d-8ad4-8503fc14610b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472746} :answer-field/id #uuid "5cfac123-c198-5997-bc78-bc4c79e3be46" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473768}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "0b65bfe0-6178-564e-825d-19d4ac9443d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-150012" :question/problem "![](images/5a/5a3961346a4bcb0d94e46caf6d6ed1253dc56fb4761db07b11829e329bc2fa8d.png)\n\nConsider the part of parabola and constant vector field $F$ shown above. Let $C$ be the path where the part of parabola is traversed from $A$ to $B.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$\n- ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ gives the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along $C:$\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statements I is false, while statement II is true. As the particle moves from $A$ to $B,$ the force $F$ works against the particle for $x>0,$ while $F$  works with the particle for $x<0.$ \n\n![](images/af/af80eab6427f376084301c03715fd098cfe4a1c816dcd72d3e1129cfa35ff29d.png)\n\n \n\nBy symmetry, the contribution to ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ for $x<0$ is canceled out by the contribution for $x>0.$ So,\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. If we reverse the orientation of $C,$ then the situation with regards to the work done by $F$ is similar to the previous case.\n\n![](images/a2/a26ca79400bf30aa891543d30a052a6e8ec071ccb48fcd8c418fe0a713dad212.png)\n\n \n\nSo, ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414785 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00c75fe3-0f58-55e1-8f86-a88338d5cfcb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472520} {:answer/id #uuid "a60b9432-a58a-5243-9f31-007a718f9157" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472521}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a60b9432-a58a-5243-9f31-007a718f9157" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472521} :answer-field/id #uuid "7ce59e55-a6c7-5acf-b0ee-3ead7fb9939a" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473655} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2f1a6c81-b372-55cc-97ce-f7cde5c58ef7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472522} {:answer/id #uuid "8cd28fc9-2509-520a-9b6e-b710a4fcd873" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472523}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f1a6c81-b372-55cc-97ce-f7cde5c58ef7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472522} :answer-field/id #uuid "69033084-6739-5ed3-8082-9c13508586c2" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473656} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f261d4a8-0a18-578f-91e8-66fc2b9fc81b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472524} {:answer/id #uuid "f8017c78-c722-5466-81ee-36047fd63b5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472525}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f261d4a8-0a18-578f-91e8-66fc2b9fc81b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186472524} :answer-field/id #uuid "149a514a-7fb2-5fae-8638-fa7be7c75462" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186473657}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "429525c1-21c9-588e-9357-69745fab8529" :question/math-academy-id "q-125488" :question/problem "![](images/f7/f712612e5cf628e2cf6f2aac5195bf98b620edee4cab1791829a4ade13bcee15.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F$ shown above, and let $C$ be the path along the segment $\\overset{―}{AB}$ traversed from $A$ to $B.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$\n- ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ gives the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along $C:$\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true, while statement II is false. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ assists the motion of the particle as it moves from $A$ to $B.$\n\n![](images/87/8726ab8c3d764016e1bfa5206769674b6809ab3ea047b03734ae5141f0b553b9.png)\n\n \nSo, ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- Statement III is false. It's clear from the picture below that if we reverse the orientation of $C,$ then $F$ works against the motion of the particle as it moves from $B$ to $A.$\n\n![](images/56/56e77c37324ca2f28c0a09d762d1e5e1f4a29f5f00695e5cbadca748d92b1c6f.png)\n\n \nSo, ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Sign of a Line Integral Over a Constant Vector Field"}]}
